         "step": 1,
         "text": "A degree 2 polynomial needs the values through order 2: \\( g(-2) = 1 \\), \\( g'(-2) = 3 \\), \\( g''(-2) = -2 \\). The value of order 3 is not used.",
         "mathjson": -2
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "Divide each by the matching factorial: \\( \\frac{1}{0!} = 1 \\), \\( \\frac{3}{1!} = 3 \\), \\( \\frac{-2}{2!} = -1 \\).",
